{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014A9m54SjgVy136VVghizRn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task carefully:\n\n1. I need to create three test files for the `pkg/sys` package:\n   - `pkg/sys/terminal_test.go` - Tests for TerminalSize, TerminalWidth, DefaultTerminalSize, IsTerminal\n   - `pkg/sys/stat_test.go` - Tests for ExtractMetadata\n   - `pkg/sys/signal_test.go` - Tests for InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize\n\n2. Key requirements:\n   - R1: Test terminal size functions with non-terminal FDs (os.Pipe)\n   - R2: Test ExtractMetadata with real temp files, verify ModTime and Blocks\n   - R3: Test InstallSIGPIPEHandler idempotency (no panic on double call)\n   - R4: Test OnTerminalResize callback registration\n\n3. Design decisions:\n   - D1: Use os.Pipe() for non-terminal FDs\n   - D2: Use t.TempDir() and os.CreateTemp for metadata tests\n   - D3: Test installation mechanics, not signal delivery\n\n4. Acceptance criteria:\n   - AC5: Use package sys (internal tests) for access to unexported state\n   - AC6: stat_test.go calls only public ExtractMetadata, no build tags needed\n\nNow I'm reviewing the sys package requirements to understand what needs to be tested, then I'll write out the test implementations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28847,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28847},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa920512-b38b-4398-a421-cfe8e29ba923","uuid":"a6d18a12-abb7-4579-af56-1102f8c476b5"}
